# LSP and retraction runtime explainer.
#
# Generates a nested HTML note for the v4 LSP/retraction design.
#
# Run from repo root:
#   cargo run --manifest-path v4/Cargo.toml --bin sprefa-run -- \
#     v4/examples/lsp-retraction-runtime-html.sprf --root . --show-rows

rule(:runtime_layers, ORD?, NAME?, TAG?, BODY?);
rule(:runtime_edges, FROM?, TO?, LABEL?);
rule(:policy_rows, NAME?, RX?, OWNER?, PROPAGATION?);

`01|Content ids|foundation|SQLite rows already get content-derived _id values. That gives the reconciler a stable row key, independent of insertion order.
02|Owner slices|missing core|Every materialized op needs an owner key: pipe hash, instance id, depth, op path, and input key.
03|Replace outputs|missing core|Rule rows, diagnostics, hovers, mounted SQL, git diff rows, and poll rows should all write through one replace-slice API.
04|Dirty deps|partly live|Reads park continuations on table, file, git, poll, or external dirty keys. Dirty keys rerun owners, not whole worlds.
05|Visible delta|core bailout|If a rerun produces the same content row ids, no downstream dirty event fires.
06|Completion boundary|runtime loop|A run drains immediate work until only parked subscriptions remain. Watchers and polls schedule future epochs.`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<ORD>[^|]+)\|(?P<NAME>[^|]+)\|(?P<TAG>[^|]+)\|(?P<BODY>.+)`
  > runtime_layers(ORD, NAME, TAG, BODY);

`LSP save|file dirty|save dispatches FILE_DOMAIN for the changed path
file dirty|read rerun|parked read continuations wake by file key
read rerun|owner rerun|stable owner key runs against new bytes
owner rerun|replace outputs|old owner slice is diffed against new rows
replace outputs|visible delta|shared rows keep support; stale rows retract
visible delta|downstream wake|only real visible changes publish table or row dirty`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<FROM>[^|]+)\|(?P<TO>[^|]+)\|(?P<LABEL>.+)`
  > runtime_edges(FROM, TO, LABEL);

`Pure memo|map|keyed by component identity and input content|cache hit returns prior node; no materialized rows
Replace slice|switchMap|stable owner key per op and input|new output set replaces old output set
Append log|mergeMap|owner key includes event id or tick id|old output remains visible
External effect|tap|not cached unless effect declares idempotence|writes dirty keys when external state changes
No-op rerun|distinctUntilChanged|same owner plus same row ids|no visible delta, no downstream wake`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<NAME>[^|]+)\|(?P<RX>[^|]+)\|(?P<OWNER>[^|]+)\|(?P<PROPAGATION>.+)`
  > policy_rows(NAME, RX, OWNER, PROPAGATION);

`v4/examples/lsp-retraction-runtime.html`
  > render.markdown`<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>sprefa LSP retraction runtime</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --ink: #17202a;
      --muted: #53606f;
      --line: #d6dde6;
      --paper: #fbfcfe;
      --panel: #ffffff;
      --blue: #2563eb;
      --green: #11835b;
      --red: #c2410c;
      --gold: #9a6a00;
      --violet: #6d28d9;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background:
        linear-gradient(180deg, #f7fbff 0%, #fffaf3 46%, #f7fff9 100%);
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }

    main {
      width: min(1180px, calc(100vw - 32px));
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 36px 0 56px;
    }

    header {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 22px;
      align-items: end;
      padding-bottom: 18px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 64px);
      line-height: 0.95;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      font-size: 22px;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); max-width: 72ch; }
    code {
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      background: #eef4ff;
      padding: 2px 5px;
      border-radius: 5px;
      color: #193b7a;
    }

    .hero-card, .panel, .layer, .policy, .edge {
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.86);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(33, 43, 54, 0.06);
    }

    .hero-card {
      padding: 18px;
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .equation {
      font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
      background: #101827;
      color: #d6e4ff;
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 14px;
      overflow-x: auto;
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      margin-top: 18px;
    }

    .panel {
      padding: 18px;
    }

    .span-7 { grid-column: span 7; }
    .span-5 { grid-column: span 5; }
    .span-12 { grid-column: span 12; }

    .layers {
      display: grid;
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .layer {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 58px 1fr;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 12px;
      align-items: start;
    }

    .num {
      font: 700 18px ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
      color: var(--blue);
    }

    .layer strong, .policy strong, .edge strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 3px;
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .tag {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      padding: 2px 7px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: #eef4ff;
      color: #1d4ed8;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .edge {
      padding: 12px;
      min-height: 116px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    .edge::after {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      right: 12px;
      bottom: 10px;
      width: 44px;
      height: 4px;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--green), var(--blue));
      border-radius: 999px;
    }

    .policies {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .policy {
      padding: 12px;
      min-height: 176px;
      border-top: 4px solid var(--green);
    }

    .policy:nth-child(2) { border-top-color: var(--blue); }
    .policy:nth-child(3) { border-top-color: var(--gold); }
    .policy:nth-child(4) { border-top-color: var(--red); }
    .policy:nth-child(5) { border-top-color: var(--violet); }

    .small-label {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .nested {
      display: grid;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    details {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 12px;
      background: #fff;
    }

    summary {
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    ul { margin: 10px 0 0 20px; padding: 0; color: var(--muted); }
    li { margin: 5px 0; }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      header, .flow, .policies { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .span-7, .span-5, .span-12 { grid-column: span 12; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <header>
      <div>
        <h1>LSP retraction runtime</h1>
        <p>A generated map for the v4 design: content keys identify rows, owner keys identify output slices, dirty deps rerun only subscribed owners, and visible deltas decide whether downstream work wakes.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-card">
        <strong>Core invariant</strong>
        <div class="equation">owner_key = H(pipe_hash, instance_id, depth, op_path, input_key)
row_key   = H(table_name, canonical_row_payload)
visible   = support_count(table_name, row_key) &gt; 0</div>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="grid">
      <div class="panel span-7">
        <h2>Foundation Layers</h2>
        <div class="layers">
${ runtime_layers?(ORD?, NAME?, TAG?, BODY?)
  > render.markdown`          <article class="layer">
            <div class="num">${ORD}</div>
            <div>
              <span class="tag">${TAG}</span>
              <strong>${NAME}</strong>
              <p>${BODY}</p>
            </div>
          </article>
`
}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel span-5">
        <h2>Replace Slice API</h2>
        <div class="nested">
          <details open>
            <summary>Type signatures</summary>
            <div class="equation">replace_outputs(owner, table, rows) -&gt; VisibleDelta
VisibleDelta { inserted_row_ids, retracted_row_ids }</div>
          </details>
          <details open>
            <summary>Instance timeline</summary>
            <ul>
              <li>LSP save or watcher emits a dirty key.</li>
              <li>Parked rows subscribed to that key rerun.</li>
              <li>Each materialized op writes a new output slice for the same owner.</li>
              <li>Store diffs old support rows against new support rows.</li>
              <li>Empty visible delta stops propagation.</li>
            </ul>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Storage reads and writes</summary>
            <ul>
              <li>Read old supports by owner key.</li>
              <li>Hash new output rows by content.</li>
              <li>Insert added supports and visible rows idempotently.</li>
              <li>Delete removed supports.</li>
              <li>Delete visible rows whose support count reaches zero.</li>
            </ul>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel span-12">
        <h2>LSP Save Flow</h2>
        <div class="flow">
${ runtime_edges?(FROM?, TO?, LABEL?)
  > render.markdown`          <article class="edge">
            <strong>${FROM} -> ${TO}</strong>
            <p>${LABEL}</p>
          </article>
`
}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel span-12">
        <h2>RxJS And Reconciler Policy</h2>
        <div class="policies">
${ policy_rows?(NAME?, RX?, OWNER?, PROPAGATION?)
  > render.markdown`          <article class="policy">
            <strong>${NAME}</strong>
            <div class="small-label">rxjs shape</div>
            <p><code>${RX}</code></p>
            <div class="small-label">owner identity</div>
            <p>${OWNER}</p>
            <div class="small-label">propagation</div>
            <p>${PROPAGATION}</p>
          </article>
`
}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="panel span-12">
        <h2>Unstaged HEAD Rule Shape</h2>
        <p>The git diff source should be a materialized relation. Its owner key stays stable for a repo and mode, so changing the unstaged file set replaces the relation slice.</p>
        <div class="equation">rule(:unstaged_head_file, FS?, STATUS?);

git.diff(:unstaged)
  &gt; unstaged_head_file(FS, STATUS);

unstaged_head_file?(FS?, STATUS?)
  &gt; path&#96;&#36;{FS}&#96;
  &gt; read
  &gt; ast[rs](...)
  &gt; lsp[warn](message = &#96;unstaged change: &#36;{FS}&#96;);</div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
`
  > write_file`v4/examples/lsp-retraction-runtime.html`;
